# What you should learn next

### 1. HL7 v2

Learn the basic message structure.

Especially:

```text
MSH
PID
PV1
ORC
OBR
OBX
```

You don't need to learn the entire HL7 specification.

Understand what an **ADT** message is first.

For example:

```text
ADT → patient admission/discharge/transfer
```

Then learn how patient information is represented inside the message.

This teaches you something very important about US healthcare:

> **FHIR is not the only format you'll encounter. Healthcare organizations have a huge amount of existing HL7 v2 infrastructure.**

---

# 2. Build an HL7 ingestion pipeline

Use Python.

Your input could be:

```text
data/
   hl7/
      message_001.hl7
      message_002.hl7
      message_003.hl7
```

Then:

```text
        .hl7 files
             │
             ▼
        Python parser
             │
             ▼
       Validation
             │
             ▼
      Normalized records
             │
             ▼
        PostgreSQL
```

